== (c) cmem:product-label ==
label update minimizes over s at fixed q_X: smallest excess = 0.00072914
cue update minimizes over q_X at fixed s: smallest excess = 0.015439
normalizer of the cue update 0.1698313168 <= sum_a s_a Z_a(o) = 0.176772325
disjoint cue supports, s = (1/2, 1/2): product of weighted densities = ['0.0', '0.0', '0.0', '0.0'] so the normalizer is 0 and every q_X has KL(q_X||mu_1) or KL(q_X||mu_2) infinite

== (d) the D06-PRED-04 example ==
Z(0) = 2.7182818284590452354  e = 2.7182818284590452354
S =             10: int over (e^-S, 1/e) of l log l du = 0.96310211 (closed form 0.96310211)
S =           1000: int over (e^-S, 1/e) of l log l du = 4.9235708 (closed form 4.9235708)
S =        1000000: int over (e^-S, 1/e) of l log l du = 11.81554 (closed form 11.81554)
S =  1000000000000: int over (e^-S, 1/e) of l log l du = 25.631021 (closed form 25.631021)
the integral of l log l diverges like log S, so KL(posterior || prior) = +inf and the separated form is +inf - (+inf) at the posterior, while KL(posterior || posterior) - log Z(0) = -1

